25-10-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"G000602","fullName":"Rep. Gillen, Laura [D-NY-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"B001323","fullName":"Rep. Begich, Nicholas J. [R-AK-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AK"},{"bioguideId":"F000477","fullName":"Rep. Foushee, Valerie P. [D-NC-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"F000472","fullName":"Rep. Franklin, Scott [R-FL-18]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:04:49+00:00","id":"hr477-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-16","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-16","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology."},"laws":[],"number":"477","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"F000480","district":20,"fullName":"Rep. Fong, Vince [R-CA-20]","party":"R","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-16","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Making Advancements in Commercial Hypersonics Act or the MACH Act</strong></p><p>This bill permits the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) to establish a research program to facilitate the testing of high-speed aircraft and related technologies, to be known as the Making Advancements in Commercial Hypersonics Program.</p><p>Within a specified time period, NASA must develop a strategic plan for such research. NASA must also consult with the Department of Defense and the Federal Aviation Administration on these efforts.&nbsp;</p><p>Under the program, NASA may not (1) fund the development of hypersonic and related technologies; or (2) enter into an agreement with certain foreign entities of concern, including entities owned or controlled by China, Iran, North Korea, or Russia.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-14T19:55:23Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"MACH Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-01-13T09:05:36Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-01-13T09:05:36Z"}
